<!--
  network.xml — the isolated libvirt network the CAPE guest lives on (#316).
  Defined directly via `virsh net-define` / `virsh net-start` (no separate
  install-network.sh wrapper yet — add one if this chain grows the same
  amount of network-lifecycle logic sandbox/ghosts's did).

  Deliberately a fourth, distinct bridge — NOT a reuse of `virbr-sandbox`
  (win11-sandbox's own network). Two independent Windows sandbox guests
  sharing one bridge would let a CAPE detonation see win11-sandbox's guest
  (and vice versa) on the same L2 segment; #316 rejected that outright, the
  same reasoning `sandbox/ghosts/network.xml` already documents for why
  GHOSTS got its own bridge instead of reusing this one too.

  No <forward> element, same as `sandbox/network.xml` (Linux runner) and
  `sandbox/windows`'s own sandbox-network.xml — this network has no route
  out. Routing-mode decision (#316): CAPE supports per-analysis
  drop/inetsim/internet/VPN, but internet/VPN are ruled out immediately by
  this repo's blanket no-outbound-network posture (same posture that
  keeps win11-sandbox and the Linux runner both routeless). Default mode
  is `drop` (matches every other detonation route's default). `inetsim`
  is supported by CAPE itself but deliberately NOT wired to the existing
  docker-compose.sandbox.yml INetSim instance shared by the Linux/Windows
  runners — two independent guests hitting one INetSim process risks
  session/state cross-contamination between unrelated detonations. A
  CAPE-dedicated INetSim instance, on this bridge's own gateway address,
  is left as follow-up work (tracked in #314's host-stack scope, not
  built here) rather than shipped half-isolated.

  10.40.50.0/24: distinct from every other range already in use on this
  host (10.8.0.0/24 wg0, 10.10.10.0/24 sandbox, 10.20.30.0/24 ghosts,
  10.90.0.0/24 ghosts_net docker, 192.168.42.0/24 LAN, 198.18.0.0/24
  virbr-hpsbx), so a routing mistake elsewhere can't silently overlap
  this one.
-->
<network>
  <name>cape</name>
  <bridge name='virbr-cape' stp='on' delay='0'/>
  <ip address='10.40.50.1' netmask='255.255.255.0'>
    <!-- No <dhcp><host> pin yet: #315's golden image (and its guest's
         MAC address) doesn't exist yet. Pin it here the same way
         sandbox/ghosts/network.xml pins win11-ghosts's, once #315 lands. -->
    <dhcp>
      <range start='10.40.50.10' end='10.40.50.99'/>
    </dhcp>
  </ip>
</network>
